{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5074300","formula":"C₈H₁₄O","hill":"C8H14O","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":14.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"1-octen-3-one"},"descriptions":{"en":"Oct-1-en-3-one (CH2=CHC(=O)(CH2)4CH3), also known as 1-octen-3-one, octeneone or amyl vinyl ketone, is the odorant that is responsible for the typical \"metallic\" smell of metals (such as coins) and blood coming into contact with skin. Oct-1-en-3-one has a strong metallic mushroom-like odor with an odor detection threshold of 0.03–1.12 μg/m3 and it is the main compound responsible for the \"smell of metal\", followed by decanal (smell: orange skin, flowery) and nonanal (smell: tallowy, fruity). Oct-1-en-3-one is the degradative reduction product of the chemical reaction of skin lipid peroxides and Fe2+."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":61346,"mass":126.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCC(=O)C=C","inchikey":"KLTVSWGXIAYTHO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"oct-1-en-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"61346","atoms":23,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.75,"y":-1.722,"z":-0.004,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.998,"y":0.467,"z":0.004,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.756,"y":-0.429,"z":0.021,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.281,"y":-0.365,"z":0.023,"el":"C"},{"x":0.546,"y":0.375,"z":-0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.518,"y":0.518,"z":-0.021,"el":"C"},{"x":1.797,"y":-0.492,"z":-0.015,"el":"C"},{"x":3.136,"y":0.163,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.324,"y":1.485,"z":0.015,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.979,"y":1.138,"z":0.872,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.982,"y":1.098,"z":-0.893,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.766,"y":-1.054,"z":0.922,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.788,"y":-1.115,"z":-0.835,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.31,"y":-0.982,"z":0.929,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.296,"y":-1.046,"z":-0.835,"el":"H"},{"x":0.56,"y":0.982,"z":-0.938,"el":"H"},{"x":0.58,"y":1.039,"z":0.846,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.535,"y":1.124,"z":-0.932